From: Gilroy Scott <gilroyscott1970@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: npu: bounce mailbox messages through a DMA-safe buffer

The NPU mailbox buffer is bidirectional: the CPU writes the request and the
NPU writes its response back into the same memory. Commit 6f884eb87a79
correctly switched the mapping to DMA_BIDIRECTIONAL so the CPU invalidates
its cache before reading the response on non-coherent CPUs.

The message buffer became a caller-side kzalloc() in c52918744ee1 ("net:
airoha: Move memory allocation in airoha_npu_send_msg() caller"); its size is
not a multiple of the cache line, so its tail shares a cache line with the
adjacent allocation. On EN7581 (non-coherent) the DMA_BIDIRECTIONAL unmap
invalidate corrupts the NPU-written response via that shared line.

Bounce the message through a cache-line-aligned buffer so the streaming DMA
maps and invalidates whole cache lines. Validated on Gemtek W1700K
(EN7581 + MT7996): version reads 0.1111, RX/TX offload work, CPU idle.

Fixes: 6f884eb87a79 ("net: airoha: Fix DMA direction for NPU mailbox buffer")
Signed-off-by: Gilroy Scott <gilroyscott1970@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_npu.c | 17 ++++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_npu.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_npu.c
@@ -165,15 +165,23 @@ static int airoha_npu_send_msg(struct airoha_npu *npu, int func_id,
 	u16 core = 0; /* FIXME */
 	u32 val, offset = core << 4;
 	dma_addr_t dma_addr;
-	int ret;
+	void *dma_buf;
+	int ret, buf_sz;

-	dma_addr = dma_map_single(npu->dev, p, size, DMA_BIDIRECTIONAL);
+	buf_sz = ALIGN(size, dma_get_cache_alignment());
+	dma_buf = kzalloc(buf_sz, GFP_ATOMIC);
+	if (!dma_buf)
+		return -ENOMEM;
+	memcpy(dma_buf, p, size);
+
+	dma_addr = dma_map_single(npu->dev, dma_buf, buf_sz, DMA_BIDIRECTIONAL);
 	ret = dma_mapping_error(npu->dev, dma_addr);
-	if (ret)
+	if (ret) {
+		kfree(dma_buf);
 		return ret;
+	}

 	spin_lock_bh(&npu->cores[core].lock);

 	regmap_write(npu->regmap, REG_CR_MBQ0_CTRL(0) + offset, dma_addr);
@@ -190,7 +198,10 @@ static int airoha_npu_send_msg(struct airoha_npu *npu, int func_id,

 	spin_unlock_bh(&npu->cores[core].lock);

-	dma_unmap_single(npu->dev, dma_addr, size, DMA_BIDIRECTIONAL);
+	dma_unmap_single(npu->dev, dma_addr, buf_sz, DMA_BIDIRECTIONAL);
+	if (!ret)
+		memcpy(p, dma_buf, size);
+	kfree(dma_buf);

 	return ret;
 }
